WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.501
 Jason, Shawn,
congratulations, you've

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.070
made it to the final
round of this competition.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.638
When you guys showed
up to the forge,

00:00:05.704 --> 00:00:08.741
we asked you to forge our judge
Ben Abbott's favorite knife,

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:10.109
the Celtic ring knife.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.845
Now, we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.079
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history,

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:16.316
from the same kilted region.

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:23.389
That weapon is-- the
Irish ring-hilted sword.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.224
 [exhales]

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:26.759
WIL WILLIS: Dating back
to the 12th century,

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:29.528
the Irish ring hilted sword
was a classic European weapon,

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:32.532
with a blade reaching
lengths of up to 40 inches.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:35.134
The broad, double-edged weapon
featured a distinctive ring

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.904
pommel that was key for
counterbalancing its weight,

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.105
allowing for swift
and deadly cuts.

00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:42.441
Commonly used by the
elite mercenaries known

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.310
as Gallowglass, the
well-balanced sword

00:00:44.376 --> 00:00:46.078
complemented their
superior fighting

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:48.648
techniques that were
revered throughout Ireland

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.182
in the Middle Ages.

00:00:50.282 --> 00:00:52.518
Although warriors such as the
Gallowglass no longer exist,

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.988
the weapon's symbolism is still
represented in popular culture

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.957
today and can be seen
on the television

00:00:58.057 --> 00:00:59.893
show "Game of
Thrones," where one

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.961
of the most feared
characters, The Mountain,

00:01:02.027 --> 00:01:04.163
wields his ring hilted sword.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.130
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:07.300
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:07.900
 Good luck.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:08.834 line:14%
 Good luck man.

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:11.971 line:14%
[rock music]

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:13.606 line:8%
SHAWN SHROPSHIRE: My
name is Shawn Shropshire,

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.007 line:14%
from Piedmont, Oklahoma.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:16.742 line:8%
I'm pretty confident
that I can win this.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:20.245
I've got a one-in-four shot
before we swing a hammer.

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:23.182
If I were to win the
money, my son has already

00:01:23.248 --> 00:01:24.450
said we're going on vacation.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.452
I would prefer to use
it for some shop tools,

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.788
so maybe we can strike a
balance between the two.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.123
[music playing]

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:33.193
OK, try to thin this
out and draw it out now.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:41.801
I'm going in for my
first heat on the steel.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.135
I go to the power hammer.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:46.039
Within about four or five
strikes, it stops on me.

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.307
If I don't get the
power hammer fixed,

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:51.544
the entire schedule that
I've had in my head for this

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.078
is out the window.

00:01:53.178 --> 00:01:54.247
Back in business.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.718
It's not perfect.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.052
There's a few things I
still need to tweak on it.

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:02.321
But I need to
start moving steel.

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:04.023
 I've never made fullers
this length before.

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:09.095
If I grind through all
the way, then it's trash.

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:10.330
I need the quench to go right.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:12.431
Because if I have
to start over now,

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:16.135
it's going to put me way behind.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.737
To catch back up to
this point and still

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.139
be able to get the
handle on the way I want,

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:21.474
I'd be pushing it to finish.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:24.277
So I really need
things to go right.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.016
I've got a little bit
of a wiggle in it.

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:31.217
The steel's hard.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.584
I've got a little
bit of a warp in it.

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:34.353
But I've got enough steel
left that I've still

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:35.755
got to grind away
that I don't think

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.156
that's going to be an issue.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.691
Should be as easy
as eating pancakes.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:41.494
I'm going to use some liquid
steel to assemble the guard.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.195
And then it's just a matter
of getting everything

00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:46.065
fitted up before it hardens.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.499
I've got the sword together.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:51.069 line:8%
It looks like a
battle-worthy weapon.

00:02:51.136 --> 00:02:53.840 line:14%
[rock music]

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.174 line:8%
JASON BROWN: My
name is Jason Brown.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.309 line:8%
And I live in Brevard,
North Carolina.

00:02:57.409 --> 00:03:01.147 line:8%
My daughters and my wife say,
man, you need to smile more.

00:03:01.213 --> 00:03:02.448
I don't know why I don't smile.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:04.550
My mom and dad spent a
fortune on my braces,

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:07.287
but I will smile if I
win "Forged in Fire."

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:12.058
Steel's moving really good.

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.292
I got a lot of work to do.

00:03:13.358 --> 00:03:15.895
But so far, I feel really good.

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.963
I have an issue with my sword.

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:20.266
It's a little thin
up by the tang.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:24.837
I want to put a few beads of
weld on it to strengthen it.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.472
[bleep]

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:30.309
This made my blade
worse than I started.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.445
Mind's sort of
flustered right now.

00:03:32.511 --> 00:03:34.614
And it kind of melted the edge.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:39.952
I'm going to do a stack weld
and build it up that way.

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:41.521
My welding finally worked.

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:46.192
I'm going to stop the weld
now and start grinding.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:49.261 line:8%
Right now, I'm engraving
Celtic runes on here.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:51.697 line:8%
This one means family,
or relationships,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:55.835 line:8%
because I've made a bunch of
new "Forged in Fire" family.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:59.238
I look forward to going back and
seeing how my blade tests out.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.041
And I'm glad it's
over right now.

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:04.744
Can finally get
some sleep, maybe.

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:08.714
 All right, bladesmiths,
this is the kill test.

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.516
To find out what
kind of lethal damage

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.886
your Irish ring hilted swords
can do, I will take your weapon

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.657
and deliver killing blows
on this feral boar carcass.

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:18.624
Jason, you're up first.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.425
You ready?

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:19.959
 I am.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:22.794
 Let's do this.

00:04:22.861 --> 00:04:26.399
[rock music]

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:39.678
All right, Jason.

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:42.181
First up, when I grab
on to it, it feels

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:44.483
good in the hands-- a good fit.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.553
Now, swinging this is sweet.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.924
You have a very sharp
edge that cuts easily

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:54.827
into this wild boar carcass.

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:56.329
It will kill.

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:57.129
Good job, Jason.

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:58.197
 Thank you.

00:04:58.263 --> 00:04:59.665
 All right, Shawn, you ready?

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:00.566
 Yes, sir.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:03.669
 Let's do this.

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:07.373
[rock music]

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:15.315
 Ooh.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.859
 All right, Shawn, let's talk
about your weapon right here.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:29.161
First up, when I grabbed
on to the handle,

00:05:29.227 --> 00:05:30.830
it's got a good feel to that.

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:32.498
I like that you put
some grooves in there,

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:34.867
because it fits nicely to
where my hand locks into it.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.835
And I get a very secure fit.

00:05:36.935 --> 00:05:41.507
A little heavier, but the
weight helps push and cut

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:44.109
into this wild boar carcass.

00:05:44.209 --> 00:05:47.146
And most of all, it will kill.

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:48.047
 Thank you, sir.

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:49.115
 Good job.

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:50.015
Ben?

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:51.918
[suspenseful music]

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:53.452
BEN ABBOTT: Welcome
to the strength test--

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:55.454
the dreaded ice chop.

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:58.290
To test the strength and
durability of your swords,

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:00.093
as well as their
overall construction,

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.061
I'm going to be chopping
mercilessly into

00:06:02.127 --> 00:06:04.097
this unforgiving block of ice.

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:05.731
Remember, this test
is all about what

00:06:05.797 --> 00:06:07.699
that ice does to your
ring hilted swords,

00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:10.302
and not what your
swords do to the ice.

00:06:10.402 --> 00:06:11.203
Jason, you're up first.

00:06:11.303 --> 00:06:11.937
You ready?

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:13.506
 Yeah, go ahead.

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:15.140
 Good.

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:18.778
[rock music]

00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:34.593
Well, Jason, first
things first, the warp--

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:38.030
I think that it being off center
made it rotate in my hand.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.400
But the balance on this sword,
as you can see, is beautiful.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.002
It's comfortable to wield.

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:44.770
And your sword held up.

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:45.304
Well done.

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:46.172
 Thank you.

00:06:46.238 --> 00:06:46.938
 Shawn, you're up.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:48.007
How you feeling?

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:49.341
 Nervous, but excited.

00:06:49.441 --> 00:06:51.010
 All right, let's do it.

00:06:56.381 --> 00:06:59.952
[rock music]

00:07:09.094 --> 00:07:09.829
 (WHISPERS) Nice.

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:15.668
 Well, Shawn, the weight on
this is a little tip-heavy.

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:18.471
I would have liked a little
bit more counterbalance on it.

00:07:18.538 --> 00:07:21.540
But that being said, it's
still a lot of fun to swing.

00:07:21.606 --> 00:07:23.075
Your edge held up beautifully.

00:07:23.141 --> 00:07:25.277
Everything's right and tight.

00:07:25.377 --> 00:07:26.078
Well done.

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:27.213
 Thank you, sir.

00:07:27.279 --> 00:07:28.480
 Next up is the sharpness test.

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:29.982
And for that, I
give you to Dave.

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:31.984
[suspenseful music]

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:34.520
 OK, gentlemen, now, to test
the sharpness of your blade,

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.355
I'll be cutting through
this sugar cane.

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:38.190
I'll use both edges
of your blade.

00:07:38.257 --> 00:07:40.559
Now, unlike the strength
test, this is all about what

00:07:40.625 --> 00:07:42.327
your blades do to that target.

00:07:42.394 --> 00:07:43.696
We want to see those
cuts nice and clean,

00:07:43.762 --> 00:07:45.598
not canes broken or
pushed out of the way.

00:07:45.664 --> 00:07:46.999
Jason, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:47.833
 I am.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:48.601
 OK.

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:57.743
[rock music]

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:08.253
All right, Jason, your handle
construction, you can see

00:08:08.353 --> 00:08:10.222
how square that is right there.

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:12.591
When that was in
my backhand cut,

00:08:12.691 --> 00:08:15.494
I actually got into those
canes, and then it rolled.

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:19.931
Your tang is now kind of
kicking off to one side.

00:08:19.998 --> 00:08:23.335
So that probably happened
as that blade caught

00:08:23.401 --> 00:08:25.938
that last cane and yanked down.

00:08:26.004 --> 00:08:29.674
But definitely a sharp
blade, really nice.

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:31.143
Shawn, you're up.
Are you ready?

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:31.877
 Yes, sir.

00:08:31.977 --> 00:08:34.480
 OK.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:38.150
[rock music]

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:44.924
 Nice.

00:08:47.727 --> 00:08:48.861
 OK.

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:51.230
First up, your handle
construction I like a lot.

00:08:51.296 --> 00:08:53.866
It's not rotating in my hand.

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:57.303
It's a heavier sword,
but the cuts are clean.

00:08:57.369 --> 00:08:58.470
It's definitely a sharp blade.

00:08:58.537 --> 00:08:59.438
I like that.

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:00.172
Well done.

00:09:00.272 --> 00:09:01.040
 Thank you.

00:09:04.009 --> 00:09:06.679
 Jason, Shawn, the judges'
deliberation is complete.

00:09:06.746 --> 00:09:08.714
They've made their
final decision.

00:09:08.781 --> 00:09:10.917
The next "Forged in
Fire" champion is--

00:09:15.187 --> 00:09:16.688
Shawn.

00:09:16.788 --> 00:09:18.958
Congratulations, you're the
new "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:19.024 --> 00:09:21.727
Jason, unfortunately, your
blade didn't make the cut.

00:09:21.827 --> 00:09:23.829
Please surrender your blade.

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:26.465
 I would have
liked to have won.

00:09:26.565 --> 00:09:28.501
But I'm proud of what
I've done, I mean,

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:31.336
throughout this whole
series of tests.

00:09:31.436 --> 00:09:32.938
I made a strong, sharp blade.

00:09:33.039 --> 00:09:36.442
And it performed equally
as well, so I mean, I'm--

00:09:36.508 --> 00:09:39.311
I'm happy with it.

00:09:39.411 --> 00:09:40.612
 Shawn, congratulations.

00:09:40.679 --> 00:09:42.114
You're the new "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:42.214 --> 00:09:45.350
And that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:46.585
How do you feel about that?

00:09:46.651 --> 00:09:47.419
 It doesn't suck.

00:09:47.519 --> 00:09:48.320
[laughter]

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:49.755
 No, it does not.

00:09:49.822 --> 00:09:53.125
 Shawn, please present
your blade to the judges.

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:54.593
SHAWN SHROPSHIRE:
This whole experience,

00:09:54.693 --> 00:09:55.661
it's pushed me physically.

00:09:55.761 --> 00:09:57.630
It's pushed me mentally.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.531
Parts of it have
been pretty brutal.

00:09:59.598 --> 00:10:00.933
Thank you, guys.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.501
And I wouldn't trade a
minute of it for anything.

00:10:02.601 --> 00:10:04.002
I've-- I've had the
time of my life.

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:07.607
[theme music]

